# pyron COSMO DISRUPTION — the maintainer's hold recipe, reached through the
# REAL PICK FLOW rather than a forced-pick poke (14z-75).
#
# WHY: forced-pick pokes load the character but do NOT run the pick flow —
# documented already for the HUD index field, which the real flow populates
# and the poke leaves reading an alias row (docs/GOTCHAS.md). If any of that
# state feeds the move, a poked rig can miss a crash that real play hits.
# This rig walks the cursor onto Pyron's cell and picks him, exactly as
# replay 40 does, then performs the move.
#
# Cursor path from the default Demitri cell 0x01 (see replay 40's header):
#   D -> 0x06 , D -> 0x08 , DR -> 0x0B , D -> 0x11
# The third press is DR, not D: the extension rewires 0x08 D to Huitzil's
# cell 0x10, so the diagonal is the route to the cell carrying Pyron's edge.
#
# Then the maintainer's 100% repro: 41236 + 2K, HELD until the move ends by
# itself. Releasing early is what made replays 71/77 miss it.
#
# Meter only (the pick is real, so no id poke):
#   POKES="3000:ff8509:09;3300:ff8509:09"
300-305 sys=C1
800-803 sys=S1
1000-1002 p1=D
1040-1042 p1=D
1080-1082 p1=DR
1120-1122 p1=D
1700-1702 p1=1
# 41236, then HOLD 2K and do not let go
3400-3402 p1=L
3403-3405 p1=DL
3406-3408 p1=D
3409-3411 p1=DR
3412-3414 p1=R
3415-3815 p1=45
5200 wait
